## Overall structure

This repo uses the **OfficeFloor YAML function-injection pattern** described in AGENTS.md, **not** Spring MVC controllers. Owner creation is the single endpoint `POST /api/owners`, wired as a pipeline of small one-public-method function classes in a YAML file, all under `govern: [ transaction ]`. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`) are generated from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`.

### YAML files under `src/main/resources/officefloor/` relating to owner creation
- `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — the create-owner pipeline (the main one).
- `src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyLimitExceededException.yml` — maps the 429 handler.
- Other owner escalations that can fire on this endpoint: `MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml`, `InvalidTelephoneException.yml`, `DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`, `DuplicateHouseholdException.yml`, `InvalidEmailException.yml`, `CityCapacityExceededException.yml`, plus generic `DataIntegrityViolationException.yml`, `MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml`, `NotFoundException.yml`, `AuthorizationDeniedException.yml`, `java.lang.Exception.yml`.

The pipeline order in `owners.POST.yml` is: validate → normalizeTelephone → normalizeEmail → ensureUniqueTelephone → ensureUniqueHousehold → ensureCityCapacity → **ensureDailyLimit** → build → **defaultRegistrationDate** → assignCustomerCode → **assignMembershipNumber** → assignHousehold → countNamesakes → save → respond.

---

## 1. Where the registration date is set/defaulted

The request **may supply** `registrationDate` (it's an optional field on the `OwnerFields` schema); when omitted it's **defaulted to the server's current date**.

- Schema definition: `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2039-2044 — `registrationDate` is optional, "defaults to the server's current date when omitted", format `date`, not in the `required` list (lines 2051-2056).
- The supplied value flows in via the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` → `OwnerMapper.toOwner(request)` in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java` lines 11-13 (MapStruct maps `registrationDate` by name; no custom mapping in `OwnerMapper.java`).
- The defaulting logic: `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DefaultRegistrationDate.java` lines 16-20:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
    }
}
```
Wired at `owners.POST.yml` lines 58-61 (step `defaultRegistrationDate`, runs after `build`). Note it uses a plain `LocalDate.now()` — no weekend/business-day rollover (relevant to test in section 4).

The `Owner` entity fields are in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` line 55 (`private LocalDate registrationDate;`), getter/setter lines 104-110.

---

## 2. Where the membership number is generated (year segment from registration date)

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java` lines 16-19:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    String yy = String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
    owner.setMembershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + yy);
}
```
Format is `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` = last two digits of the registration-date year (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`). It depends on both the customer code and the registration date being set already, hence its wiring at `owners.POST.yml` lines 73-76 (after `assignCustomerCode` and `defaultRegistrationDate`, before `save`).

Supporting: the customer code (the `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` prefix) is generated in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` lines 19-26. `membershipNumber`/`customerCode` entity fields: `Owner.java` lines 58, 61 (getters/setters lines 112-125). Schema descriptions: `openapi.yml` lines 2090-2099.

---

## 3. Where the daily create-limit counts owners per day

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureDailyLimit.java` lines 18-31:
```java
static final long MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100;

public void service(OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyLimitExceededException {
    LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
    long todayCount = 0;
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate())) {
            todayCount++;
        }
    }
    if (todayCount >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY) {
        throw new DailyLimitExceededException(MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY);
    }
}
```
It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and rejects at 100/day with a 429. Note it runs **before** `build`/`defaultRegistrationDate` (`owners.POST.yml` lines 46-49), so it counts against the server's today, independent of any `registrationDate` supplied in the request body.

